Here's something fun:  Best game I've ever had (isn't it always?),
with adventures down to level 41, via level teleport traps.  However,
I have yet to find a single scroll of teleport.  That's right, folks.
I've got luckstones, artifacts out my ass (ouch!), every potion and
other scroll, wands galore, every tool, lots o' genocides, yellow
dragon scale mail, but no scroll of teleport.  I can't get down to the
interesting levels of Hell, now that I've used up the level teleport
traps.  Growf.

It's one thing not to win because the Mazes of Menace are dangerous.
That's ok.  It's something else again not to win because the Mazes of
Menace are boring.

Here's a proposal:  Put in a little code that will *guarantee* that at
least one unidentfied scroll and potion will show up on each new
level.  The wands and rings and amulets are less common, and not as
necessary to the completion of the game, but those teleport scrolls
are essential.  By the time you've seen as many levels as there are
scrolls, you're guaranteed to have seen all the scrolls.

It also would be nice to guarantee:  at least one altar per alignment,
appearance of all the special levels (rogue and bigroom, in addition
to medusa and stronghold), one beehive, one barracks, one zoo, a
couple of kitchen sinks, one temple, one oracle, and so on.  Also, a
certain amount of random shops would be nice, though not essential.
The character I mentioned only had two, and was invisible right away,
so didn't go into either on them on the way down (a pickaxe solved
that problem).

